1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,367
9:01? No sense of time.

2
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:07,400
The elevator wouldn't come! This isn't late. So what~

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,333
Per policy, you clocked in at 9:05. And that coffee is still warm.

4
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:16,100
They're late: no sense of time. I'm late: the elevator. Double standard, number one.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,300
I'm… Modapman.

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,300
Case summary. Take-your-kid-to-work day. Location: Dad's office.

7
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,800
Dad, I got a visitor badge! What do you do at work?

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,367
I'm a deputy manager. Pretty important around here.

9
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,733
HR. I'll be your guide today.

10
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:36,467
Psst, could you say something nice about me in front of my kid…

11
00:00:36,467 --> 00:00:38,033
Per policy, I only state facts.

12
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:40,600
Just three rounds. Round one: annual leave.

13
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,467
Mr. Kim's off on a Friday again? Just tacking it onto the weekend.

14
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:46,133
Dad, what's annual leave?

15
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:49,467
Paid days off for working hard. I'm taking Monday.

16
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:53,633
Gotta stretch the weekend to recharge. So what~

17
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:57,933
They stretch the weekend: a trick. I do it: recharging. Double standard, number two.

18
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:02,267
Leave is taken when the employee asks, in principle. Fridays, Mondays, either one.

19
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:04,233
So Mr. Kim's Friday is fine too?

20
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:08,700
Then I will take Friday AND Monday! A four-day weekend!

21
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,733
Round two: messages after work.

22
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:14,267
A message at 11 p.m.? I'm off the clock! Not cool!

23
00:01:14,267 --> 00:01:16,533
Honey, what did you just send to Mr. Kim?

24
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:19,700
That one says "see it tomorrow." Just sharing info~

25
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:24,533
…Asleep already? At 11? No passion at all.

26
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:29,167
They text late: rude. I text late: sharing info. Double standard, number three.

27
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:31,967
Sir, I couldn't sleep after your message last night.

28
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:35,867
When others do it, it's their character. When you do it, it's the situation. Actor–observer bias.

29
00:01:35,867 --> 00:01:37,733
Actor… what?

30
00:01:37,733 --> 00:01:40,700
Round three: success is mine, failure is yours.

31
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,500
This quarter's results? I set the direction, you know.

32
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,300
(in a fake crowd voice) All thanks to our deputy manager~! You are the best~!

33
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:48,533
This time… the team just didn't keep up.

34
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:52,100
Success: me. Failure: them. Double standard, number four.

35
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,700
Wins are my skill, losses are someone else's fault. It's called self-serving bias.

36
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,500
For the record, Mr. Kim's name is on page one of that proposal.

37
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,033
…Huh?

38
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:02,300
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

39
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:07,267
Them late to a meeting: no manners. Me: the last meeting ran long!

40
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:10,633
Their long lunch: slacking. Mine: networking!

41
00:02:10,633 --> 00:02:14,767
Their slow reply: lazy. Mine: careful review!

42
00:02:14,767 --> 00:02:18,033
Double standard: five, six, seven!

43
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:21,433
Dad, there were so many people at your work.

44
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,133
Yeah. Everyone's busy.

45
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:29,333
Your boss, Mr. Kim… at home, they're somebody's dad, somebody's mom.

46
00:02:29,467 --> 00:02:34,133
…You're right. I should say sorry to Mr. Kim.

47
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:37,533
A pudding with no name? Community property~ So what.

48
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:38,733
…That's mine.

49
00:02:38,733 --> 00:02:43,167
Someone else eats it: theft. I eat it: shared. Double standard, number eight.

50
00:02:43,167 --> 00:02:45,933
Per policy… that is MY pudding!!

51
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:48,633
The name was under the lid. Just a wrong answer.

52
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:51,033
(instantly calm again) Per policy, this will be reflected in your performance review.

53
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:52,967
…Classic Modapman.
